---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PUBLIC_COMPANY_NAME, PUBLIC_EMAIL, PUBLIC_PHONE, WHATSAPP_URL } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Notice & Contact Information" description="How HAN XING handles submitted inquiries, website activity and business contact information.">
  <article class="procurement-page procurement-privacy">
    <section class="procurement-hero"><div class="container procurement-privacy-wrap"><p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy</p><h1>Privacy notice</h1></div></section>
    <div class="container procurement-privacy-wrap procurement-privacy-body">
      <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-23">23 October 2026</time>. This notice explains how we handle inquiries and website activity, and how to contact us about your information.</p>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-drafts"><h2 id="privacy-drafts">Submitting an inquiry</h2><p>The <a href="/contact/#inquiry-form">contact form</a> sends your name, company, email, optional phone number, country, selected products and requirements to our server when you select <strong>Send inquiry</strong>. A success message and reference are shown only after the inquiry has been saved. Product or guide references may accompany your request.</p><p>Submitted inquiries are stored in a restricted database for reviewing requirements and following up. Only authorised administrators can view or export them. We do not store what you type before submitting the form or record keystrokes.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-message"><h2 id="privacy-message">Email and WhatsApp</h2><p>You can contact <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_EMAIL}</a> or WhatsApp {PUBLIC_PHONE} directly. These services process the messages you send under their own terms. Clicking a contact link does not tell us whether you sent a message and is not counted as a received inquiry.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-technical"><h2 id="privacy-technical">Website activity</h2><p>We use visitor identifiers in cookies and browser storage to recognise visits and returning visitors. We record page and product views, specification and image interactions, download and contact clicks, form starts and submission outcomes. Records include a timestamp, page path, product, website language and button position. If you submit an inquiry, we can link these visits to the name and contact details you provide.</p><p>Where available, Cloudflare supplies an approximate country. We infer device category and recognise sources from referrer hostnames and source / medium campaign labels. We do not store full referrer URLs, search queries, raw IP addresses or form values in analytics events. Rate limiting uses keyed hashes. An unavailable country or source remains unknown. Tracking failures do not prevent browsing or submitting an inquiry.</p><p>Cloudflare Turnstile protects online submissions. Cloudflare may process technical information to validate a request. Hosting providers may also keep access and security logs.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-business"><h2 id="privacy-business">Business contact</h2><p>{PUBLIC_COMPANY_NAME} is the business contact listed on this website. See the <a href="/about/#supplier-records">company page</a> for the address and contact details.</p><p>Email <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_EMAIL}</a> or contact <a href={WHATSAPP_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp · {PUBLIC_PHONE}</a>.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-questions"><h2 id="privacy-questions">Questions about your information</h2><p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_EMAIL}</a> to ask how your correspondence is used or retained, request correction or deletion, or ask to stop follow-up messages.</p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
